    {
      "id": 18,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "6. Service SLI — as the alert rules compute it",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 53
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "SLI ratio: proportion meeting per-class threshold",
      "description": "Placeholder. The SLI is a ratio against per-class latency thresholds, and those are null in slo.yaml until they are calibrated; this panel keeps its id because the burn-rate rules will point at it.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 54
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "The SLI query arrives when plan 3 freezes the class thresholds (slo.yaml)."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "7. Derived panels — read these with the two headline metrics",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 58
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 23,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "CPU saturation",
      "description": "CPU seconds burned per second (by task), over the 0.25 vCPU Fargate ceiling. 1.0 is the ceiling: a task pinned at or above it is CPU-bound regardless of what the pool or the database says. READ IT ONE WAY ONLY: that is sufficient evidence of CPU-bound, never necessary. http.server.cpu.duration sums only the bracketed synchronous block in src/handlers.js (feed's summarize); JSON serialisation, pg driver work and the OTel export are uncounted, and routes that bracket nothing contribute no series at all. A task can be genuinely pinned while this panel reads low.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${prometheus_datasource_uid}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 59
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${prometheus_datasource_uid}"
          },
          "expr": ${jsonencode(cpu_saturation_ratio)}
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "unit": "percentunit"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 24,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Event-loop delay p99 by task",
      "description": "nodejs_eventloop_delay_p99_seconds, by (instance): one line per task. A rising delay here with CPU saturation flat says only that the loop had pending work the CPU accounting does not see; it does not say what kind. Read it beside the pool row: requests parked waiting for a connection are pending callbacks, not compute.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${prometheus_datasource_uid}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 59
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${prometheus_datasource_uid}"
          },
          "expr": ${jsonencode(eventloop_delay_p99)}
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
